> 
> I've had this happen on the OS/2 version of NetHack. Start deleting
> files in the bones directory from the last modified.

That isn't it, though, because there are no bones files.  It happens from a
fresh install.  It has something to do with compression, I think, because
with I compile with the compression option turned completely off, I get a
core dump when trying to back up a level.  But if I use Huffman compression
(i.e., "pack"), it returns the message "Read 2055 instead of 529209 bytes"
and then "Abort".  "compress" gets me that "EOF on file #4" error.

